  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Playing the Game",
    "section": "1.77",
    "heading": "Ranged Attacks in Close Combat",
    "lineStart": 671,
    "lineEnd": 673
  },
  "section": "1.77",
  "rulesText": "Aiming a ranged attack is more difficult when a foe is next to you. When you make a ranged attack roll with a weapon, a spell, or some other means, you have Disadvantage on the roll if you are within 5 feet of an enemy who can see you and doesn't have the Incapacitated condition (see “Rules Glossary”)."
}
